  "id": "solomon-four-group-design",
  "term": "Solomon four-group design",
  "definition": "Solomon four-group design is an experimental research design used to test an intervention while also checking whether giving a pretest affects the results. In the packet, it is used by comparing experimental groups that receive gamification-supported teaching with control groups that do not, with some groups pretested and others not.",
